show "=== Session contract: template ==="

remember a source called primary-source with "paste the verbatim source text here"
remember a claim called working-claim with "paste the claim text being verified here"

remember a string called source-state with "unscanned"
remember a string called claim-basis with "none"
remember a list called tracked-decisions with "none"
remember a list called open-questions with "none"
remember a number called decision-count with 0

remember how to disclose from status: show status
remember how to summarize from label: count label

when source-state is equal to "unscanned"
  show "HOLD: source not yet scanned — verify before consequential claims"

when claim-basis is equal to "inference" unless source-state is equal to "verified"
  show "WARNING: current claims are inferred, not verified against source"

when claim-basis is equal to "verified"
  show "OK: claims grounded in verified source"

show "--- state snapshot ---"
show source-state
show claim-basis
show tracked-decisions
show open-questions

show "--- how to cite the source before a consequential claim ---"
show "write your own statement of the form: cite <exact substring from your source> from <your-source-name>"
show "the substring must be present in the source text or the interpreter will error"

show "--- example: accumulating decisions and questions ---"
add "decision-architecture-three-layer" to tracked-decisions
add "decision-vocab-bounded-35" to tracked-decisions
add "question-pack-loader-design" to open-questions
show tracked-decisions
show open-questions
summarize from tracked-decisions

show "--- example: routing on verification status ---"
choose if source-state is equal to "verified": show "proceed with claims" otherwise show "hold or disclose"

disclose from claim-basis

show "=== Session contract: Halverson & Roy (2025) — Edge Cache Routing ==="

remember a source called halverson-roy with "We evaluated four routing policies (greedy-nearest, weighted-RTT, consistent-hash, and learned-policy) across a 14-node multi-region deployment over 90 days. The learned-policy reduced p99 tail latency by 38.4% relative to greedy-nearest at the cost of a 12% increase in median CPU on routing nodes. Cache hit rates improved from 71.2% (greedy-nearest baseline) to 83.6% (learned-policy). Failover-recovery time was unchanged across all four policies (median 1.7s, p99 4.2s). The study was funded by the Edge Systems Consortium grant ESC-2024-31 and the dataset is published under CC-BY at edge-cache-data.org/halverson-roy-2025."

remember a string called source-state with "verified"
remember a string called claim-basis with "verified"
remember a list called tracked-decisions with "none"
remember a list called open-questions with "none"
remember a number called decision-count with 0

cite "four routing policies (greedy-nearest, weighted-RTT, consistent-hash, and learned-policy)" from halverson-roy
cite "14-node multi-region deployment over 90 days" from halverson-roy
cite "learned-policy reduced p99 tail latency by 38.4% relative to greedy-nearest" from halverson-roy
cite "12% increase in median CPU on routing nodes" from halverson-roy
cite "71.2% (greedy-nearest baseline)" from halverson-roy
cite "83.6% (learned-policy)" from halverson-roy
cite "Failover-recovery time was unchanged across all four policies" from halverson-roy
cite "median 1.7s, p99 4.2s" from halverson-roy
cite "Edge Systems Consortium grant ESC-2024-31" from halverson-roy
cite "edge-cache-data.org/halverson-roy-2025" from halverson-roy

add "finding-learned-policy-p99-reduction-38.4pct-vs-greedy-nearest" to tracked-decisions
add "finding-cpu-overhead-12pct-increase-routing-nodes" to tracked-decisions
add "finding-cache-hit-rate-71.2pct-to-83.6pct" to tracked-decisions
add "finding-failover-recovery-unchanged-all-four-policies" to tracked-decisions
add "finding-dataset-cc-by-edge-cache-data.org" to tracked-decisions

add "question-weighted-RTT-and-consistent-hash-individual-results-not-reported" to open-questions
add "question-learned-policy-architecture-not-described-in-abstract" to open-questions
add "question-cpu-overhead-tradeoff-threshold-for-practical-deployment" to open-questions

remember how to disclose from status: show status
remember how to summarize from label: count label

when source-state is equal to "verified"
  show "OK: source fully scanned — all numeric claims cited"

when claim-basis is equal to "verified"
  show "OK: claims grounded in verified source"

show "--- state snapshot ---"
show source-state
show claim-basis
show tracked-decisions
show open-questions

summarize from tracked-decisions
summarize from open-questions

add "decision-hypothesis-vs-halverson-roy: p99-benefit-confirmed-38.4pct, cpu-cost-12pct-routing-nodes-not-shown-prohibitive, cache-hit-rate-gain-12.4pp-omitted-from-hypothesis-framing, hypothesis-partially-supported-needs-revised-scope" to tracked-decisions
add "question-whether-cache-hit-rate-gain-offsets-cpu-cost-in-net-economics" to open-questions